@title Turbine Telemetry Pipeline
@subtitle Skerry Wind Power, 6 offshore wind farms, region eu-north-1
@author Asset Data team, Owner
@date 2026-10-02

kpi Wind farms | 6
kpi Peak ingest | 18,000 msg/s | 24 shards
kpi Uplink buffer | 6 h | then oldest dropped | bad

## Overview
Turbine readings flow from each farm into one central stream and are processed once.
They are then split into a fast store for dashboards and a cheap archive for audits.

## Pipeline diagram
diagram pipe dir=TB title="Telemetry pipeline"
pipe: ctrl "Turbine Controllers" svc
pipe: gw "Edge Gateway" svc "buffers 6 h on disk" focus
pipe: stream "Telemetry Stream" queue "24 shards"
pipe: proc "Stream Processor" fn focus
pipe: ts "Timeseries Store" db
pipe: raw "Raw Archive" store
pipe: alert "Alerting Service" svc
pipe: dash "Operations Dashboard" user
pipe: ctrl -> gw : OPC UA, 1 Hz
pipe: gw -> stream : MQTT over TLS, batched every 5 s
pipe: stream -> proc : consumer
pipe: proc -> ts : 10 s aggregates
pipe: proc -> raw : Parquet every 15 minutes
pipe: proc -> alert : threshold breach
pipe: ts -> dash : queries
pipe: group site "On site at each farm (outside cloud account)" ctrl, gw
pipe: group cloud "Cloud account, eu-north-1" stream, proc, ts, raw, alert, dash
pipe: legend

## Capacity and retention
table = Component,Size,Retention; Telemetry Stream,"24 shards, 18,000 msg/s at peak",—; Timeseries Store,—,"7 days in memory, 3 years on magnetic storage"; Raw Archive,—,"10 years, cold storage after 90 days"

## If the uplink fails
!!! The Edge Gateway buffers at most **6 hours** of readings on disk. After 6 hours the **oldest readings are dropped** and cannot be recovered.
- While the link is down, the gateway writes readings to local disk.
- When the link returns, it replays buffered readings **in order**.
- An outage longer than 6 hours means a permanent gap in the data: escalate before the limit is reached.
